INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Zero-Day Vulnerability in MOVEit Transfer Exploited for Data Theft / CISA advisory page", "source_url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-158a", "text": "SRC-001 reports that Progress announced CVE-2023-34362 on May 31, 2023. Mandiant observed earliest exploitation on May 27, 2023, with web-shell deployment and data theft, sometimes within minutes. The campaign targeted MOVEit Transfer; actors deployed a newly discovered C# web shell named LEMURLOOT, often masquerading as legitimate human.aspx, with samples human2.aspx and _human2.aspx. Exploitation involved POST requests to guestaccess.aspx consistent with SQL injection. LEMURLOOT could enumerate files/folders, retrieve configuration and Azure Blob settings, retrieve files, and create/delete a Health Check Service user. Scanning/exploitation often came from 5.252.188.0/22; second-stage interaction/data theft came from different systems. Many supporting hosts exposed RDP and had certificates generated May 19-22, suggesting staged infrastructure. Mandiant initially attributed activity to UNC4857, then on June 6 merged UNC4857 into FIN11 based on targeting, infrastructure, certificate and data leak site overlaps. A June 6 CL0P^_-LEAKS data leak site post claimed responsibility and threatened publication unless an extortion fee was paid; a June 5 Bleeping Computer report said someone affiliated with CLOP claimed responsibility. Mandiant linked the activity to prior FIN11 data-theft extortion via the CL0P^_-LEAKS site and noted overlaps in ISPs, netblocks and IPs, including an exploitation IP used by FIN11 from mid-January 2023 with the same RDP service/certificate. Mandiant had not directly observed extortion emails to confirmed victims at publication, and described delayed extortion contact as plausible based on prior FIN11 operations. The campaign affected organizations in Canada, India and the U.S., with likely broader impact; LEMURLOOT samples were also uploaded from Italy, Pakistan and Germany. SRC-002 states CVE-2023-34362 is an unauthenticated SQL injection in MOVEit Transfer allowing database access and potentially inference, alteration or deletion of database elements; unpatched systems could be exploited via HTTP/HTTPS, and exploitation occurred in May/June 2023. NVD lists publication date June 2, 2023, CISA KEV addition June 2, 2023 with due date June 23, 2023, required action apply vendor updates, CVSS 3.1 9.8 Critical, CWE-89."}
